            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n> (Am I missing something? How are other people dealing with this?)\r\n\r\nYes, kind of. `<CR>` is also commonly customizable in \"autopairs\" type of plugins, like 'mini.pairs'. [This is mentioned](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b1af49d98233180c6045e81f4aef5b663d032b62/doc/mini-completion.txt#L147-L150), So having it as default will go against using 'mini.pairs' (as it would still require the whole mapping from scratch) or other autopair plugin. Having it by default also respect 'mini.pairs' but not others (as I don't really want to mix them in 'mini.completion') doesn't look fair.\r\n\r\nI have an idea of incorporating this into the future 'mini.keymap', i.e. have something like `map_super_tab()`, `map_super_shifttab()`, and `map_super_cr()` which will track popular ways of using those keys in Neovim community.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned (as part of 'mini.completion').",
