        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks @echasnovski for the explanation. I just have one follow-up question: don't you think that the fact that `<CR>` sometimes dismisses the menu with an actual `<CR>`, and sometimes it does not, is a bug *somewhere*, maybe in neovim itself?\r\n\r\nIn particular I have this reproducer:\r\n\r\n1. Set the mini.completion `delay = { completion = 250 }` as it makes things easier\r\n2. Open a new empty text file, type `foobar` in it, then on a new line type `fo` quickly.\r\n   1. The completion menu appears\r\n   2. Press `<CR>`, the menu is dismissed and a `<CR>` is added to the buffer\r\n3. Now on a new line type `f`, wait for the menu to appear, type `o`.\r\n   1. Everything seems identical as before\r\n   2. Press `<CR>`, the menu is dismissed, but a `<CR>` is **not** added to the buffer\r\n\r\nThis doesn't seem right to me?",
